{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2017-514", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/514", "wordCount": 2135, "segments": [{"start": 17.0, "text": "Hello, welcome to our session"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "on error handling best practices"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "for HTTP live streaming."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "My name is Shravya Kunamalla and"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "I am an AVFoundation engineer."}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "Let's get started."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "There are a huge number of Apple"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "developers streaming content"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "using our very popular HTTP live"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "streaming."}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "Over the years, the usage has"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "evolved into multiple complex"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "delivery scenarios."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "The developers are doing live"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "event broadcasts, prerecorded"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": ", and in each of"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "these there are possibly"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "multiple different media"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "selections, variance at"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "different bit rates, audio and"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "subtitles of different"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "languages."}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "The content itself might be"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "protected and there could"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "possibly be millions of"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "simultaneous viewers subscribing"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "to your streams."}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "Given the enormity the system is"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "bound to run into errors."}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "A lot of developers and content"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "providers have asked us one"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "question in particular over the"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "years, what is the right thing"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "to do when an error happens."}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "And on very popular demand, we"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "present to you today the best"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "practices for handling errors on"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "both app and the server side."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "Most of you listening to this"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "talk might already know all"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "about HLS delivery, but let's"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "quickly go through the overview."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "We have a master playlist, this"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "consists of alternate versions"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "of the same presentation."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "In this example, there is a 6"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "megabit and 2 megabit video,"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "English and French audio,"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "English and French subtitles."}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "Each of these is called a media"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "playlist and has its own"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "playlist."}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "The media playlist consists of"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "segments."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "In case of life, the segment"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "list is updated at regular"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "intervals on playlist re-fetch."}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "The segments may be dropped off"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "from the beginning and new"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "segments are added to the end."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "In case segments are protected"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "media playlist also contains"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "keys."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "We also have session data, this"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "can be for example titles or"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "lyrics."}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "These are the resources that the"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "server is expected to deliver"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "and the HLS client needs for"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "playback."}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "So, what should the server do"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "when it's unable to deliver due"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "to errors?"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "What are the best practices for"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "handling both content and"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "delivery errors?"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "There are a number of iOS,"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "macOS, and tvOS clients"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "expecting resources from server."}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "The server should aim to deliver"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "the resources in time and if it"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "fails to do so, communicate the"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "right error code to AVPlayer."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "This error code should clearly"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "convey the cause of error."}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "Was the request a valid request,"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "was it authorized, has the"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "server encountered an error?"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "Is the server incapable of"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "performing the request, for"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "example due to an unsupported"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "feature request?"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "Next, let's see the recommended"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "way to signal these various"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "errors to AVPlayer."}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "So, here is the list of failures"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "and the recommended error codes."}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "These are in compliance with the"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "standard HTTP error codes"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "specified in RFC7231."}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "Segments are protected and the"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "AVPlayer does not have the"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "required authentication, send"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "401."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "If the client doesn't have"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "authorization for the content,"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "send 403."}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "For all temporary resource"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "unavailable cases like"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": ", send 404."}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "For permanent resource"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "unavailability, send 410."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "For all unexpected server"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "conditions where no other"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "specific message applies, send"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "500."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "Most of the content providers or"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "CDNs are cache in proxies which"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "are getting the content itself"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "from some encoder somewhere."}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "To notify of invalid response"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "from gateway, send 502."}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "If server is down for"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "maintenance or overloaded and is"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "unavailable for any other"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "reason, send 503."}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "For gateway timeout, send 504."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "Now these error codes aren't"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "necessarily new they have been"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "around for a while."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "And if we look closer at these"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "errors there is a class of"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "errors that are temporary like"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "resource and server temporary"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "unavailability."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "Starting iOS 11 we now have a"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "way to explicitly communicate"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "such temporary failures to"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "AVPlayer by means of GAP tag."}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "We mark segments as GAP by the"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "use of EXT-X-GAP tag."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "This can be applied to one or"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "more segments."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "Put this in your playlist to"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "indicate GAP and enable AVPlayer"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "to make an informed decision."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "On seeing this tag AVPlayer will"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "know that this is a temporary"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "failure and may decide to go to"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "a backup alternate or switch"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "down."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "If nothing viable is available"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "in the utmost case AVPlayer will"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "play the available media until"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "we recover from the error"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "condition."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "So, going back to failures and"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "error codes."}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "For which of these errors is the"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "GAP tag applicable, 404"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "temporary resource"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "unavailability and 503 server"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "unavailability always use GAP"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "tag. Keep in mind, this tag is"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "applicable to both live and"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "playback, but the"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "use case is typically the live"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "scenario."}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "Next, let's move on to HLS"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "specific media error cases."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "On live playback, the HLS pack"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "specifies that the playlist"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "needs to be updated on regular"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "intervals."}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "If the server is unable to"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "update the playlist in time"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "according to the published"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "target duration, we recommend to"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "communicate the stale playlist"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "to AVPlayer by sending 404."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "Now returning stale playlist"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "itself is fine, but that leaves"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "the onus of identifying the"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "stale playlist on the AVPlayer"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "which it does eventually."}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "And on identifying that AVPlayer"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "will try to recover by means of"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "switching to other available"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "or retries."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "This may be too late in some"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "cases leading to stalls."}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "Sending 404 instead will"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "communicate the stale playlist"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "to AVPlayer much more quickly."}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "There is another advantage here,"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "it would also give immediate"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "notification of stale playlist"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "to any new AVPlayer joining the"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "stream. For unsupported features for"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "example, BYTE-RANGE not"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "supported, send 501."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "For all authentication failures,"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "send 401."}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "Next, an example going through a"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "typical live playback scenario."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "Let's say we have two video"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "variants, one of 6 megabit and"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "one of 2 megabit."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "We also have the responding"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "encoder packagers one providing"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "6-megabit content and another"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "providing 2-megabit content to"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "our server."}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "And the server is distributing"}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "this content to the HLS client"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "requesting it."}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "Let's say the"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "bandwidth of the app is good"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "enough to handle the 6-megabit"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "variant it goes ahead and"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "fetches the 6 megabit media"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "playlist."}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "Gets the response back and moves"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "on to fetch the first segment,"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "segment one."}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "Everything seems to be good"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "until now."}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "Then suddenly the 6-megabit"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "encoder or packager is down with"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "substantial downtime for"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "example."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "The next time AVPlayer"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "re-fetches the playlist the"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "server now has a way to"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "communicate the failure to it,"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "GAP tag."}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "For this re-fetch request, we"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "recommend that server should now"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "send 200 okay and the subsequent"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "segments in the media playlist"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "should be marked as GAP."}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "AVPlayer on seeing this GAP tag"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "switches down to 2-megabit"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "variant media playlist and moves"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "on to fetch the next segment,"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "segment two, from the 2-megabit"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "variant."}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "With this we have switched down"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "smoothly and in time to avoid a"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "stall."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "For backward compatibility for"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "any segment request marked as"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "GAP the server should still send"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "404."}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "Next, let's move on to failover."}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "What is a failover?"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "It is a method of protecting the"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "system from failure in which a"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "standby or backup system takes"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "over when the main system fails."}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "So, what failover can our server"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "have?"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "One viable approach is to have"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "redundant variants on backup"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "servers, have variants on"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "different servers with same bit"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "rate an include them in the"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "master playlist."}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "This will give the AVPlayer the"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "ability to smoothly switch over"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "in case of error."}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "Backup alternates will be tried"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "first before switching down."}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "If the server wants to"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "explicitly trigger a failover it"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "should send 404 to okay list"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "request."}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "To summarize, always notify the"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "HLS client of error with correct"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "error code."}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "Have backup playlists on"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "different servers to failover in"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "case of server failures, having"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "some redundancy is good."}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "Send 501 for unsupported"}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "features."}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "And in the case of live, update"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "the playlist in time as"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "specified by HLS Spec. Prefer"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "GAP tag in case of temporary"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "failures."}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "And send 404 to indicate stale"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "playlist."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "Next, let's move on to how to"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "handle AVFoundation errors."}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "When an error occurs, the user"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "viewing the actual stream wants"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "to know two things."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "First, that the error happened"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "and second, what caused the"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "error to happen."}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "And not all errors can be"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "anticipated on the server."}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "The AVFoundation client or app"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "should be returned to respond"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "appropriately to various error"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "conditions originating from the"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "AVPlayer."}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "So, how can we identify the"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "error? The error can be identified by"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "looking at AVPlayer.status and"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "AVPlayerItem.status."}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "This will change to"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "AVPlayerStatsFailed and"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "AVPlayerItemStatusFailed"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "respectively on error."}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "For the exact error that caused"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "the status to change to fail"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "look at AVPlayerItem.error."}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "This describes what caused the"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "item to be no longer playable."}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "Listen to AVPLayerItemFailedTo"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "PlayToEndTimeNotification to get"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "notified that the item did not"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "play to end."}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "The user info dictionary of this"}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "notification contains an error"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "object that describes the"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "problem and can be retrieved by"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "AVPlayerItemFailedTo"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "PlayToEndTimeErrorKey."}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "Dig deeper, look at"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "AVPlayerItem.errorLog."}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "This gives the snapshot of all"}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "the error events that happened"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "during the playback session."}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "So, what do these errors mean?"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "They can mean one of these four"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "things, network errors,"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "timeouts, format errors, and"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "live playlist update errors."}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "Network errors are all the 4xx"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "and 5xx errors that server sends"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "and TCP/IP, DNS errors."}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "After requesting a resource"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "there are timeouts for each"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "master playlist, media playlist,"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "medial files, and keys."}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "And failure to get a response"}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "within this timeout will cause"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "timeout errors."}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "Any incorrect format of playlist"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "key and the session data will"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "result in format errors."}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "And in case of live, playlist"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "needs to be updated according to"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "published target duration and"}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "the failure to do so will cause"}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "live playlist update errors."}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "What are the corresponding AVFoundationDomain error codes?"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "For network errors and timeouts,"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "it will be AVErrorContent"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "IsUnavailable or AVErrorNo"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "LongerPlayable."}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "AVErrorContent"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "IsUnavailable indicates that the"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "content was never playable."}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "This could mean authentication"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "failures or authorization"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "failures."}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "AVErrorNo"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "LongerPlayable indicates that"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "the content was playable, but"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "over the course of time one or"}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "more errors happened resulting"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "in being no longer playable."}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "AVErrorFailed ToParse indicates parsing"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "failures."}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "AVErrorContent"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "NotUpdated means the playlist"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "was not updated in time."}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "Always look at the user info of"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "the error to get the underlying"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "error."}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "Keep in mind, this can be nested"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "if more than one error caused"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "the item to fail."}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "When a new error log entry is"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "added to error log"}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "AVPlayerItemNewError"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "LogEntryNotification is sent."}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "So, listen to this for immediate"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "notification of error."}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "I would like to stress on one"}, {"start": 906.0, "text": "point here, AVPlayer will try"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "its best to continue playback by"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "means of retries and switching"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "to different available variants."}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "The AVPlayerItem.status will"}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "change to fail only when there"}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "is no viable variant to use to"}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "continue playback and we have"}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "played out whatever buffer we"}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "have."}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "For all temporary errors,"}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "AVPlayer will attempt switching"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "and/or retry."}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "If there is nothing to switch to"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "AVPlayer will retry for a"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "reasonable amount of time before"}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "giving up."}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "After a given amount of time it"}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "will attempt to switch back up"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "to failed variant if the network"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "conditions are suitable."}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "For permanent errors like 410 no"}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "retries will be attempted and"}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "AVPlayer only tries switching to"}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "a different variant."}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "The permanent and temporary"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "error codes are in compliance"}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "with the standard HTTP error"}, {"start": 966.0, "text": "codes specified in RFC7231."}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "All session data errors are not"}, {"start": 975.0, "text": "fatal and not ignored."}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "Next, let's go to a code"}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "snippet."}, {"start": 985.0, "text": "To view the error, once you have"}, {"start": 987.0, "text": "done the usual things, create"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "your asset, create your player"}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "item, create a player with that"}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "item the first thing you should"}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "do is add observer to track the"}, {"start": 997.0, "text": "status of the player."}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "Then add observer to track the"}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "status of player item."}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "And here you register to listen"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "to AVPlayerItemFailed"}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "ToPlayToEndTimeNotification."}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "Once you have that and the"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "status of the item changes to"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "failed look at"}, {"start": 1023.0, "text": "AVPlayerItem.error to print out"}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "what the error is."}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "This is the place where you"}, {"start": 1028.0, "text": "should add code to display"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "relevant messages about the"}, {"start": 1031.0, "text": "error to the user."}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "On getting AVPlayerItemFailedTo"}, {"start": 1038.0, "text": "PlayToEndTimeNotification"}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "extract the error as the value"}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "of AVPlayerItemFailedTo"}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "PlayToEndTimeErrorKey and again,"}, {"start": 1047.0, "text": "take appropriate action."}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "For instance, print the error or"}, {"start": 1050.0, "text": "display relevant error messages"}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "to the user."}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "To summarize, always monitor"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "AVPlayer and"}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "AVPlayerItem.status."}, {"start": 1064.0, "text": "Listen to notifications,"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "AVPlayerItemFailedTo"}, {"start": 1067.0, "text": "PlayToEndTimeNotification tells"}, {"start": 1069.0, "text": "you when the item did not play"}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "to end."}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "If you want to more actively"}, {"start": 1073.0, "text": "monitor the errors for example,"}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "for the purpose of sending debug"}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "info to server for analytics"}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "listen to AVPlayerItemNewError"}, {"start": 1082.0, "text": "LogEntryNotification to know"}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "when a new error log entry is"}, {"start": 1086.0, "text": "added."}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "In conclusion, when an error"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "occurs always take appropriate"}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "action, don't ignore it."}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "Notify the user of the error and"}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "always, always display"}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "meaningful messages or pop-ups"}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "when suitable."}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "For more information, go to the"}, {"start": 1106.0, "text": "WWDC site and use the session"}, {"start": 1108.0, "text": "number 514."}, {"start": 1111.0, "text": "Thank you and have a great"}]}
